<title>FRANCE: French adj July current a/c surplus 98 mln Ffr. [corrected 08:48 gmt]</title>
<headline>French adj July current a/c surplus 98 mln Ffr. [corrected 08:48 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 98 million francs in July, down from an unrevised 8.18 billion in June, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first seven months of 1996 was 58.57 billion francs, compared with a 59.38 billion surplus in the same period a year earlier.  </p>
<p>The finance ministry gave the following unadjusted balance of</p>
<p>payments figures: (figures in billion francs unless specified)</p>
<p>					    July     June     May 96</p>
<p>   Current account (adjusted) 98 million    8.18     6.91</p>
<p>(Corrects adjusted current account figure for July from 0.98 to</p>
<p> 98 million francs)</p>
<p>   Current account		     8.55     3.19     8.60</p>
<p>   Merchandise trade		   7.81     6.78     6.95</p>
<p>   Services				9.96     7.84     3.81</p>
<p>   -- Travel			     8.90     6.51     4.52</p>
<p>   Other goods and services	  0.60     0.50     0.40</p>
<p>   Income				 -1.78    -4.93     2.82</p>
<p>   -- Investment income	     -2.70    -5.78     2.03</p>
<p>   Transfers			    -8.04    -6.99    -5.37</p>
</text>
